1
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:18,830
Airflow in a biological safety cabinet, or BSC, can be interrupted, altered, and changed

2
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:21,590
by many different factors.

3
00:00:21,590 --> 00:00:27,470
These interruptions can lead to potential exposures and or product contamination.

4
00:00:27,470 --> 00:00:30,150
This is a smoke generator.

5
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:35,590
It is used to demonstrate how airflow is affected by operations inside and around

6
00:00:35,590 --> 00:00:37,790
a BSC.

7
00:00:37,790 --> 00:00:42,310
But first, let's look at what proper airflow looks like.

8
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:48,070
For proper containment, air is drawn into the cabinet at the opening and then down into the

9
00:00:48,070 --> 00:00:49,550
front grille.

10
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:56,770
Together, the sash and inward flowing air provide an air curtain or barrier that is intended

11
00:00:56,770 --> 00:01:01,710
to keep cabinet air and room air separate from one another.

12
00:01:01,710 --> 00:01:07,310
To protect the work product, the cabinet's downward air is cleaned by a high-efficiency

13
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:09,590
filter within the cabinet.

14
00:01:09,590 --> 00:01:15,270
Upon reaching the work surface, roughly half of the downflow air moves toward the front

15
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:20,670
grille and the other half moves toward the back grille.

16
00:01:20,670 --> 00:01:25,870
The physical location of the BSC can affect the airflow as well.

17
00:01:25,870 --> 00:01:31,390
Placing a BSC too close to a doorway can cause the air to be drawn out of the BSC when

18
00:01:31,390 --> 00:01:33,070
a door is open.

19
00:01:33,070 --> 00:01:40,630
Placing a BSC too close to an HVAC supply vent can also interfere with the BSC containment.

20
00:01:40,630 --> 00:01:46,110
Proper sash height is critical because when the sash is kept at the proper height, the

21
00:01:46,110 --> 00:01:50,310
appropriate inward airflow can be maintained.

22
00:01:50,310 --> 00:01:55,930
The proper sash height is designated in the BSC operation manual and should be clearly

23
00:01:55,930 --> 00:01:58,930
indicated on the BSC.

24
00:01:58,930 --> 00:02:04,290
The performance at the BSC at the declared sash height is actually part of the cabinet

25
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:07,050
certification process.

26
00:02:07,050 --> 00:02:13,730
If the sash is too low, inward air velocity will increase at the opening, which can cause

27
00:02:13,730 --> 00:02:19,930
turbulence and potential contamination inside the cabinet.

28
00:02:19,930 --> 00:02:24,770
If the sash is set too high, an alarm will sound.

29
00:02:24,770 --> 00:02:30,150
This indicates the inward air velocity may slow down to a point that it cannot provide

30
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:33,510
and maintain containment at the sash opening.

31
00:02:33,510 --> 00:02:39,590
This could cause contaminated air to leak out of the cabinet or room air to enter the BSC

32
00:02:39,590 --> 00:02:45,870
opening, mix with the downflow air, and potentially contaminate the work product.

33
00:02:45,870 --> 00:02:52,350
Even when the sash height is correct, the air barrier at the opening is fragile, approximately

34
00:02:52,350 --> 00:02:56,930
100 feet per minute, or 1 mile per hour.

35
00:02:56,930 --> 00:03:00,090
It can be easily disrupted.

36
00:03:00,090 --> 00:03:04,730
Something as simple as the way you withdraw your arms or a person walking too close to

37
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:10,530
the cabinet can pull air and potential contaminants out of the cabinet and into the breathing

38
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:14,610
zone of the person working in the BSC.

39
00:03:14,610 --> 00:03:20,490
One common mistake is overloading the inside of the BSC with too much equipment and or

40
00:03:20,490 --> 00:03:26,750
supplies, or covering the front or rear grills.

41
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:32,430
Another way to disrupt airflow is by using a flame inside the cabinet.

42
00:03:32,430 --> 00:03:35,350
This is not a good idea for two reasons.

43
00:03:35,350 --> 00:03:41,350
One, the heat from the flame can cause air currents inside the BSC and interfere with

44
00:03:41,350 --> 00:03:43,430
proper airflow.

45
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:49,470
And two, flames are a fire hazard and can damage the HEPA filter.

46
00:03:49,470 --> 00:03:53,850
For these reasons, flames should not be used inside a BSC.
